 r←IsUsageDataFilename name
⍝ Returns 1 when `name` is the name of a usage data file, like "usage-data-2024.zip" or
⍝ "usage-data-2025-08.csv", and 0 otherwise.
⍝ The log folder these files live in holds the application log as well, and nothing but the
⍝ usage data files is for the outside world. Being that strict also rules out any path.
⍝ A line break is refused on its own account: ⎕S would otherwise look at every line separately.
 r←0
 :If ~∨/name∊⎕UCS 10 13
     r←1=≢'^usage-data-[0-9]{4}(-[0-9]{2})?\.(csv|zip)$'⎕S 0⊣name
 :EndIf
